# armour/shared/pauldron_plate_R: the medium plate pauldron (family plate, size 3: 2 px past the 16 px shoulder line
# facing right and left, 1 px facing down and up (i2: the knights' LOCO/RUN atlases, B10)),
# shared by the man and the woman (decision D10): a domed cop with one lit ridge and a glint on the lit (near, screen-left)
# one, and a lower lame under a shadow line. Over the near arm (armNear), behind the torso with the far arm (the compositor
# moves a `side` part to armFar on the far side). It rides the shoulder anchor (the lean and the bob exactly); `up` lifts it
# a pixel for overhead wind-ups; `lie` lays the near cop flat (no lower lame) and drops the far one under the body
# (the lying clip names pauld=lie; SLICE-DOLL's clip line). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
role pauldron plate.3
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R

view D key rest origin 2 2
